# Installing Aspartik

Aspartik is distributed as a Python package, so it can be installed by
any tool which supports Python: `pip`, `conda`, or `uv`.

Note that Aspartik requires Python version of at least 3.14 or higher.


## Plain `pip`

If you have `pip` and Python of an appropriate version, for example in a
[virtual Python environment][venv], you can simply install the package:

```sh
$ python --version
Python 3.14.2
$ pip install aspartik
```


## `conda`

Conda works with `pip` packages, but they must be installed in a
separate environment, not the base one.  A Conda environment with the
required Python version can be created with the `conda create --prefix
./env python=3.14` command.  You can then install the necessary Conda
packages.  Note that `pip` must be installed last.  Then it can be used
as usual:

```sh
$ conda install package1 package2 ... pip
$ pip install aspartik
```

See [_Installing pip packages_][ipp] from the Conda documentation for
more detail.


## `uv`

[`uv`][uv] is the recommended way to install Aspartik.  You can create a
virtual environment with the correct python version with `uv venv
--python 3.14`.  And install Aspartik using [`uv pip`][up].

```sh
$ uv pip install aspartik
```


[venv]: https://docs.python.org/3/library/venv.html
[ipp]: https://www.anaconda.com/docs/getting-started/working-with-conda/packages/pip-install
[uv]: https://docs.astral.sh/uv/
[up]: https://docs.astral.sh/uv/pip/
